    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Ms. Spencer is a 28-year-old charity worker, nine weeks into treatment for bulimia nervosa and depression, who comes for her yearly preventive visit. She is in week nine of CBT-E, now once a week, and takes fluoxetine 60 mg each morning. Binge eating and vomiting have fallen from about ten times a week to once or twice a week, and she eats breakfast and lunch on most days as planned with the dietitian. Her mood is better and she sleeps through most nights; her PHQ-9 today is 7. She has not yet seen a dentist, which she has put off from embarrassment, and agreed today to book an appointment. Her periods are regular. She is not sexually active and is not planning a pregnancy. She has had no thoughts of suicide or self-harm. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Visit</td><td>Periodic adult preventive visit, age 28</td></tr><tr><td>Bulimia nervosa</td><td>Week nine of CBT-E; binge eating and vomiting once or twice a week, from about ten</td></tr><tr><td>Mood</td><td>Better; PHQ-9 7; item 9 scored 0</td></tr><tr><td>Medicines</td><td>Fluoxetine 60 mg each morning</td></tr><tr><td>Dental care</td><td>Not yet seen; appointment to be booked</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Health risk assessment. Completed by the patient on a tablet in a private room and reviewed with her by Dr. Castleford. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Self-rated health</td><td>Fair and improving</td></tr><tr><td>Psychosocial</td><td>Close friends; meaningful work; has told one close friend about the treatment</td></tr><tr><td>Substance use</td><td>AUDIT-C 1; no drugs; no laxatives, diuretics, or diet pills</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco</td><td>Never smoked</td></tr><tr><td>Physical activity</td><td>Swims or goes to the gym three times a week, not to make up for eating</td></tr><tr><td>Nutrition</td><td>Three meals and two snacks on most days; coffee down to one cup a day</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>Seven to eight hours on most nights</td></tr><tr><td>Sexual and reproductive health</td><td>Not sexually active; regular periods; no pregnancy planned</td></tr><tr><td>Safety at home</td><td>Feels safe; no one hurts, threatens, or controls her; no firearm in the home</td></tr><tr><td>Road safety</td><td>Always wears a seat belt</td></tr><tr><td>Activities of daily living</td><td>Independent</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

