    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Periodic adult preventive visit completed</content>. Health risk assessment reviewed and the prevention plan updated. Cervical screening is current. She was counseled to take folic acid and will start an over-the-counter tablet. Teeth are sensitive and the enamel erosion is unchanged; the dental examination advised at intake has not happened yet. [S]<list><item>Book a dental examination this month; the clinic gave her a list of dentists.</item><item>Over-the-counter folic acid 0.4 mg daily.</item><item>Next preventive visit in one year.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Bulimia nervosa, severe (F50.23)</content>. Improving on CBT-E and fluoxetine: binge eating and vomiting once or twice a week, from about ten. [S]<list><item>Continue CBT-E weekly and fluoxetine 60 mg each morning.</item><item>Three-month review in four weeks with electrolytes.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Major depressive disorder, recurrent, moderate (F33.1)</content>. PHQ-9 7, from 14 at intake. Safety reviewed: no thoughts of suicide or self-harm; the safety plan and the 988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline are in her phone; no firearm. [S]<list><item>Continue fluoxetine 60 mg.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Personalized prevention plan. A written copy was given to the patient. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Blood pressure screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>106/68 mmHg</td></tr><tr><td>Depression screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-9 score 7, from 14 at intake; item 9 scored 0</td></tr><tr><td>Unhealthy alcohol use screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>AUDIT-C score 1</td></tr><tr><td>Intimate partner violence screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Negative; she feels safe</td></tr><tr><td>Cervical cancer screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Normal cytology two years ago; repeat cytology next year (every three years from 21 to 29), then a primary HPV test every five years from 30</td></tr><tr><td>Folic acid</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Counseled to take 0.4 mg daily as a person who could become pregnant; she will start an over-the-counter tablet</td></tr><tr><td>HIV screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Negative test three years ago; no new risk</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis C screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>No result on record; once-in-a-lifetime test drawn today with her agreement</td></tr><tr><td>Chlamydia and gonorrhea screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Age 28 and not sexually active</td></tr><tr><td>Dental examination</td><td>Due</td><td>Advised at intake because of enamel erosion from vomiting; not yet done; she will book this month</td></tr><tr><td>Influenza vaccine</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Given last autumn; next dose due this autumn</td></tr><tr><td>COVID-19 vaccine</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Current-season dose last autumn</td></tr><tr><td>Tetanus, diphtheria, and pertussis</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Tdap five years ago</td></tr><tr><td>HPV vaccine</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Series completed in adolescence</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Guideline basis: Eating disorders: recognition and treatment (NICE guideline NG69) (2017, updated 2020); VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for Assessment and Management of Patients at Risk for Suicide (2024); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, depression, bipolar, and mood disorders monograph (2026); Medicare Preventive Services reference: visit templates, screening cascades, and documentation elements (2026); USPSTF A and B Recommendations (2026); Adult Immunization Schedule by Age (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Hepatitis C result by phone. Dental examination this month. Three-month review in four weeks with electrolytes and the PHQ-9. Next preventive visit in one year. Next scheduled visit 1990-05-11: three-month review: binge and purge frequency, electrolytes, dental care, mood, and safety. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

